  "visual_findings": [
    "Revisited high pitch 280 us and yaw 80 us, then tested one additional 80-us yaw edge to 160 us. The body and other hand commands stayed at reference; tiger remained OFF.",
    "At the added yaw level a change of the active gimbal/frame outline is visible in the wider oblique view, while the high hand attachment has little clear lateral displacement. This is qualitative visual evidence, not shaft feedback or a diagnosed transmission fault.",
    "High-pose leverage, passive arm reach, connection slack and load-dependent constraint remain possible explanations. No three-dimensional kinematic mapping has been measured.",
    "Returned yaw before lowering pitch. The figure shows posture variation during return, followed by recovery toward the low pose. Exact endpoint repeatability is not established.",
    "No completed overhead crossing or same-side hand endpoint; no obvious rod interference in the viewed regions. All six stages reviewed and normally stopped at the original commands."
